{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. And let me tell you, the reality is even more captivating. I recently spent two weeks exploring this incredible country, and it completely stole my heart.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. From the vibrant Shibuya crossing to the tranquil Meiji Jingu Shrine, the city seamlessly blends tradition and modernity. I spent days wandering through quirky neighborhoods like Harajuku and Akihabara, indulging in delicious ramen and exploring themed cafes.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. This ancient capital offered a completely different vibe. I explored stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion) and Fushimi Inari-taisha with its thousands of red torii gates.  Wandering through Gion, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha, felt like stepping back in time.\n\nBeyond the major cities, I explored smaller towns, soaking in the local culture and enjoying the breathtaking scenery.  The food was consistently amazing – from fresh sushi to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was a delight. \n\nJapan is a country of contrasts, where ancient traditions coexist with cutting-edge technology. It's a place that challenges your perceptions and leaves you wanting more.  I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0011703077470883727}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968507617712021}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.10784334689378738}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.18911860883235931}, {"token": "Japan